Z||000003||LarryB||06-11-2001||11:44 AM||||The original recommendation from GM was to use a good-quality 5W-30 oil.  They subsequently updated their recommendation to use GM Synchromesh.  <P>1 quart of Synchromesh costs about the same as a 12 quart case of name brand 5W30.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||penetrator||06-11-2001||11:48 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LarryB:<BR><B>The original recommendation from GM was to use a good-quality 5W-30 oil.  They subsequently updated their recommendation to use GM Synchromesh.  <P>1 quart of Synchromesh costs about the same as a 12 quart case of name brand 5W30.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>GM knows how to make money =)<P>But do you think it is a good idea to change to 5w30 engine oil such as Castrol or something. And what kind should i have, syntethic or mineral oil?<P>I must stop the hoorible noise from the tranny. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||88CoupeV6||06-11-2001||11:55 AM||||Only stuff I use is Redline MTL Better than Motor oil or Synchromesh. I've<BR>been using it for a wile. Smoothes the shifting right out.<P>Read about it here <A HREF="http://www.redlineoil.com/redlineoil/mtlti.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.redlineoil.com/redlineoil/mtlti.htm</A> <P>------------------<BR>Josh <B>(known by TheFiero64 for first 1239 posts)</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||3
Z||000006||Scott||06-11-2001||12:00 PM||||I use Mobil 1 synthetic.  Redline is probably a little better, but the Mobil 1 is readily available and relatively cheap.<BR>||||reg||1
