Z||000008||Formula88||06-11-2001||01:02 PM||||My question is, is the Redline or the GM Synchromesh compatible with Engine oil?  I've got 5W-30 in my Getrag now, but want to switch to Synchromesh.  How important is it to fully drain the tranny?  You still have about .2-.5 quarts in there afer draining from the drain plug.||||reg||1
Z||000009||PAUL88GT||06-11-2001||02:47 PM||||Syncromesh is about $10 per quart and I had to go to the local GM dealer to find it. It is my first time to use it. It better be good for that price.<p>[This message has been edited by PAUL88GT (edited 06-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||theogre||06-11-2001||07:05 PM||||Fresh oil in the tranny is always a good thing.<P>All motor oils currently on the market exceed the original specifications for either engine or tranny in Fiero. (At least in the U.S.. I would expect the same in most of Europe.)<P>If you are changing oil then change oil. Don't mix syncromesh or anything else with the old oil. You won't get the benifit of new oil if the old junk is still in there.... <P>If you can't get the GM syncro or red line then any good motor oil should work.<P>The jury is still out on synthetic oil in the tranny. There have been posts here in the past from people who didn't like it. Others like it just fine. It probably depends just what synth is used.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Rodney||06-12-2001||08:47 AM||||If the trans makes a horrible noise I doubt any oil will cure it. Replace or rebuild.||||reg||1
Z||000012||penetrator||06-13-2001||09:39 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rodney:<BR><B>If the trans makes a horrible noise I doubt any oil will cure it. Replace or rebuild.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The funny(or not funny) thing is that it only makes noise when i have been driving like 50 kilometers with the 4th gear and then changing down to 3rd or 2nd gear, and no noise on the 4th. But i did a test, i drived 50 kilometers with only the 3rd gear, and then i changed to 2nd gear, no noise, no noise on any gear. ??? So why does the 4th gear make the other one to noise badly?<P>And when the noise starts, its gone again after like 5 minutes when im driving in the city. <P>If the tranny is gone, i guess i'll sell my car as junkparts(or what its called). A new tranny in Sweden will cost plenty of dollars, not to mention the job to change it. =(<P>thanks<BR>Magnus ||||reg||1
